Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2, virtio-gpu: zero copy in full screen by default, tiled guest buffers, guest checks

On top of 0005 (2026-10-03; measured on a 4K 240 Hz screen, see docs/RESULTS.md):

- Full screen shows the guest's display and nothing else: the ImGui menu bar
  is hidden there (the window keeps the docked choice; a dialog still shows
  over the guest; the menu hotkey in full screen leaves full screen).
- Zero copy only in full screen by default, where the guest's buffer goes to
  the screen as it is (KWin scans it out); in a window the host composites
  anyway.  QEMU_SDL_ZERO_COPY=always: in a window too, and below a docked menu
  bar on a wl_subsurface (viewporter + fractional-scale-v1 for its size and
  place; pixel-exact, but slower in full screen than a copy KWin scans out
  with the bar in it: KWin has to composite bar and subsurface).
- A second swap target, x-vblank-swap-target-zc, for frames that go to the
  screen neither copied nor composited: the display tells the device when
  (GraphicHwOps gl_zero_copy, trace virtio_gpu_zero_copy), the regulator
  starts over from the other target at each switch.
- Tiled guest buffers: QEMU_SDL_ZC_TILED=explicit derives the modifier from
  the buffer's amdgpu metadata the way the kernel's
  convert_tiling_flags_to_modifier_gfx9 does (pipe and packer bits from the
  compositor's own modifier that agrees; GFX11), so the guest no longer
  needs linear scanout buffers; a buffer with DCC goes without a modifier
  (implicit) unless =explicit-dcc (its planes derived too, not yet seen on a
  guest); =1: all tiled buffers implicitly.
- Guest buffers are created with zwp_linux_buffer_params_v1.create and a
  round trip: KWin answers a failed create_immed with a protocol error.
- Guest checks: the device records whether each scanout flush carries a fence
  it can hold (GraphicHwOps gl_flush_fenced); a guest without one is copied
  (one warning); a guest that flushes buffers the host still holds (3 in
  10 s: its compositor does not wait for the reader fence) turns zero copy
  off for the run.
- A menu painting over the guest is copied while it shows (it was not drawn
  at all with zero copy before).
- The status bar says "zero copy"; the direct/composited vote counts guest
  buffers and starts over when full screen changes.
- Presentation feedback of a subsurface's commits (sdl2_stats_present_begin_on).

Not committed in the fork yet; generated with diff on top of 0001-0005.

